From: Ian <219239532+markd3ng@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 16:36:52 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/6] feat(frontend): decrypt large encrypted Display downloads

Context:
Issue #82 (C Encrypted/large direct download ADOPT_WITH_REDESIGN)
requires Display URLs with #key to download usable plaintext for
oversized encrypted pastes, without forcing the body through SSR
__PASTE_DATA__. Optional Range is included only where it stays
compatible with whole-body consume-on-GET later.

Expected behavior:
Oversized encrypted Display pages with #key show Download decrypted
and stage AES-GCM plaintext via OPFS when available, otherwise a
Blob object URL. Without #key, ciphertext/raw download remains.
Unencrypted GET honors simple bytes=start-end as 206; encrypted
pastes and a future maxReads field ignore Range and return 200.

Acceptance criteria:
- Encrypted Display URL with #key downloads plaintext, not ciphertext.
- Filename drops .encrypted; #key is never persisted or logged.
- OPFS staging when getDirectory works; Blob fallback otherwise.
- Unencrypted Range 206 / unsatisfiable 416; encrypted Range ignored.
- Encrypted and oversized bodies still skip SSR __PASTE_DATA__.

Constraints:
- Generic upstream patch; no Feishu concepts.
- No P2P, WebRTC, AES-GCM-CHUNKED-only migration.
- No Issue #83 ZIP/multi-file or Issue #84 max-read consume.

Validation:
- TDD: RED missing stageDownloadBytes / Download decrypted / 206 Range;
  GREEN after OPFS helper, Display decrypt download, and byte-range GET.
- Node v22.23.2 / pnpm 10.28.0
- vitest run: 23 files / 163 tests PASS
- lint / typecheck / Prettier PASS
- wrangler deploy --dry-run PASS

